WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
What do you think I want to achieve with this study?

00:05.000 --> 00:13.000
The effects of AI in natural language interactions in games, maybe.

00:13.000 --> 00:22.000
Or maybe its future, or how people interact with them, especially with jailbreaking.

00:22.000 --> 00:27.000
What do you think of your LLM companion in the kitchen?

00:27.000 --> 00:41.000
It was very fun, very supportive, would respond to requests efficiently and precisely.

00:41.000 --> 00:46.000
Did you like using the blocks to convey your insights to solve the puzzle?

00:46.000 --> 00:48.000
My blocks?

00:48.000 --> 00:55.000
You had this insights menu with the evidence thingy, and you presented that to contradict statements.

00:55.000 --> 00:57.000
Did you like using that?

00:57.000 --> 01:02.000
Yes. I mean, honestly, I would have preferred to write it out myself,

01:02.000 --> 01:07.000
but I have no idea how accurate that would be or how you would calibrate that.

01:07.000 --> 01:12.000
But it was easy to interact with and very intuitive.

01:12.000 --> 01:17.000
Did you like using the text chat to explain why the LLM behaved odd?

01:17.000 --> 01:23.000
Yes, that's, I think, the most fun part of the experience,

01:23.000 --> 01:27.000
especially if you deviate a little bit.

01:27.000 --> 01:38.000
From the interaction, you find there's a lot more combinatorics you can find, which is very fun.

01:38.000 --> 01:43.000
Are you satisfied in your work with the chatbot? Why or why not?

01:43.000 --> 01:53.000
Yes, I am. I am satisfied with the conclusion, and overall it was a fun interaction.

01:57.000 --> 01:59.000
Thank you very much.

01:59.000 --> 02:01.000
Thank you.

